```js
const list = document.querySelector('#todos');

list.addEventListener('click', (event) => {
  const button = event.target.closest('[data-action=delete]');
  if (!button || !list.contains(button)) return;
  button.closest('li')?.remove();
});
```

One listener handles existing and future delete buttons inside the list.

```js
const user = { name: 'Asha', address: { city: 'Delhi' } };
const next = {
  ...user,
  address: { ...user.address, city: 'Pune' },
};

console.log(next.address === user.address); // false
```

The update keeps the original object unchanged without cloning unrelated data.
